<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese bond report.</title>
<headline>Portuguese bond report.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Futures were gaining slightly, following Spain, but the cash market could barely summon up the energy to trade.</p>
<p>The market was expected to remain apathetic in the absence of any stimulus to business, either internal or external.</p>
<p>Traders said that the lack of volatility elsewhere in Europe was influencing the longer-end, while the short-end was becalmed by the absence of internal news.</p>
<p>&quot;It is going to be a neutral day with prices holding at Friday's levels,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>----Sergio Goncalves, Lisbon burea 3511-3150035</p>
